{"availability":"available","full":"scale-tone/cognitive-search-static-web-apps-sample-ui","name":"cognitive-search-static-web-apps-sample-ui","description":"A simple sample UI for your Azure AI Search index. Built with React, TypeScript and Azure Static Web Apps","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":25,"forks":31,"created":"2020-09-02T08:52:28Z","updated":"2025-01-09T22:39:57Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["azure-ai-search","azure-cognitive-search","azure-search","azure-static-web-apps","react","typescript"],"demo":"https://calm-cliff-07e291203.5.azurestaticapps.net/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:42.741Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:42.741Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:42.741Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T20:15:42.741Z","stars":25,"forks":31}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A simple sample UI for your Azure AI Search index. Similar to this official sample, but is implemented as a Azure Static Web App and built with React and TypeScript. Implements the so called faceted search user experience, when the user first enters their search phrase and then narrows down search resuls with facets on the left sidebar.","The client part is a typical React-based SPA (Single-Page App) written in TypeScript with extensive use of MobX and Material-UI. And it doesn't have a backend as such, all requests to Azure AI Search REST API are transparently propagated through an Azure Function, that appends the Azure AI Search api-key to each request - so the api-key is not exposed to the clients.","Queries made by user are also reflected in the browser's address bar. This serves three purposes: makes those links sharable, enables navigation history (\"Back\" and \"Forward\" buttons) and also helps you learn Azure AI Search REST API's query syntax."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/scale-tone/cognitive-search-static-web-apps-sample-ui/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"9007f39d30cb1843824b0f417dc26dd4eb1359ba9e490c19025f3b0f45e4832a","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:42.852Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:42.852Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A simple sample UI for your Azure AI Search index. Similar to this official sample, but is implemented as a Azure Static Web App and built with React and TypeScript. Implements the so called faceted search user experience, when the user first enters their search phrase and then narrows down search resuls with facets on the left sidebar.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/scale-tone/cognitive-search-static-web-apps-sample-ui/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"optional","text":"AzureMapSubscriptionKey - (optional) a subscription key for your Azure Maps account (Azure Maps is used for visualizing geolocation data).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/scale-tone/cognitive-search-static-web-apps-sample-ui/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Also, when using Microsoft Accounts, you might want to configure and use your own AAD application (instead of the global default one).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/scale-tone/cognitive-search-static-web-apps-sample-ui/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"User's authentication/authorization relies entirely on what Azure Static Web Apps offer today, and that in turn relies on what is known as EasyAuth server-directed login flow.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/scale-tone/cognitive-search-static-web-apps-sample-ui/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"9007f39d30cb1843824b0f417dc26dd4eb1359ba9e490c19025f3b0f45e4832a","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/scale-tone/cognitive-search-static-web-apps-sample-ui/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:42.852Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2025-01-09T22:39:57Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceU